Derived files, and what is taken
--------------------------------

    guest/src/sim.rs
        Transliteration of upstream `lib/src/sim.rs`. Every gate arm and the measurement-coin
        protocol are upstream's semantics, including the HMR/R conditioning added in upstream's
        post-review v2. The condition stack is upstream's except that an unbalanced
        PopCondition is fatal here rather than ignored. Adapted to a packed operation
        encoding, with gate accounting folded into the same dispatch arm as execution.

    guest/src/ops.rs
        The operation format and `OperationType` discriminants follow upstream
        `lib/src/circuit.rs`. `validate_one` is a transliteration of upstream `Op::validate`,
        including its BANNED / ALLOWED / REQUIRED field policy; it additionally range-checks
        operands against the layout, bounds `r_target`, and refuses `DebugPrint`. The register
        composition rules follow upstream `program/src/main.rs`, and additionally require the
        register slots to be distinct. The packed encoding and the streaming analyser are not
        upstream's.

    guest/src/curve.rs
        `add` and `mul_reference` are transliterated from upstream
        `lib/src/weierstrass_elliptic_curve.rs`, including the affine formulae and the encoding
        of the point at infinity as (0, 0). `mul_generator` is not upstream's.

    guest/src/main.rs
        The proof procedure — commit to the circuit, derive test inputs from its hash, simulate,
        assert resource bounds — follows the design of upstream `program/src/main.rs`. The
        Fiat-Shamir derivation is byte-identical to the ecdsa.fail evaluator's by necessity: a
        proof computed over any other transcript would certify a different test set than the
        benchmark draws. The check is recorded in `provenance/evaluator-check.txt`.

    host/tests/curve_parity.rs
        Contains a second copy of the upstream curve arithmetic above, as the reference oracle.

    host/tests/validation.rs
        Includes `guest/src/ops.rs` textually, and so carries the derived code named there.

Everything else is original to doubleAI.

Changes
-------

The derived files have been modified: transliterated to a different operation encoding,
restructured so that gate accounting cannot diverge from gate execution, and extended with
validation beyond upstream's. They are not upstream's files and should not be attributed to
upstream as shipped.

